From: "Phase1 Draft (Claude, for Terhi review)" <draft@local>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 15:18:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] refactor(decode_fields): extract the PriorVAE decoder
 application into new bstpp/decode_fields.py (eq. 22, the prior-side surrogate
 substitution -- kept as its OWN module, separate from likelihood.py, because
 the guide treats the surrogates as a distinct layer from the discrete
 likelihood eqs. 23-27). Rewires ALL THREE previously independent copies:
 spatiotemporal_hawkes_model, spatiotemporal_LGCP_model, and
 Point_Process_Model.simulate() (whose copy still carried the commented
 arg-order-swapped vae_decoder_spatial remnant, now gone). exp(sp_var_mu)
 lives INSIDE decode_spatial_field with a calibration-convention docstring
 (Appendix C: restores the log-amplitude factored out during VAE training;
 computational convention, not a modeling commitment, not a sampled prior) so
 no caller can apply the gain inconsistently. NAMING NOTE: the module was to
 be decoders.py but bstpp/decoders/ is the pretrained-ARTIFACT package
 directory and shadows any sibling module -- a live naming collision
 discovered on import; hence decode_fields.py. New
 tests/test_decode_fields.py: equality with direct vae_functions application,
 calibration-gain contract f(mu)=exp(mu-mu0)f(mu0), finite gradients w.r.t. z.
 Verified: 35/35; value AND gradient pins bit-identical; fixed-seed cox_hawkes
 simulate() byte-identical before/after (3200 events, exact array equality) --
 the decode path is deterministic, so the RNG stream is untouched. Phase 2a
 complete. Deliberate deviation from the review's recommended set, recorded:
 no event_log_likelihood / background_log_rate_at_events wrappers -- the ell_1
 expressions remain visible in the model fns for the same transparency reason
 the loglik-subtraction wrapper was rejected; they have no reuse case yet
 (revisit if held-out evaluation moves off-trace in Phase 3).

